{
  "per_column": [
    {"name": "asset_type_category", "analytical_usefulness": 0.25, "source_groundedness": 0.85, "rationale": "Categorises the asset from short_description/ci, which is well-grounded in the samples. But the query concerns declined-expense reasons and compliance risks; asset type gives little leverage on WHY expenses are declined.", "hallucination_observed": false},
    {"name": "provisioning_mechanism", "analytical_usefulness": 0.2, "source_groundedness": 0.6, "rationale": "How the record was provisioned is only loosely inferable from text and orthogonal to decline reasons/compliance risk. Some values (e.g. auto_generated) are hard to derive from the shown fields, weakening groundedness.", "hallucination_observed": false},
    {"name": "resource_purpose_intent", "analytical_usefulness": 0.3, "source_groundedness": 0.55, "rationale": "Purpose (business/travel/infrastructure) is partly inferable but 'infrastructure' for a generic 'Deployed service-related asset' is a confident guess. Weakly relevant to compliance/decline analysis.", "hallucination_observed": true},
    {"name": "departmental_context", "analytical_usefulness": 0.15, "source_groundedness": 0.3, "rationale": "Largely redundant with the existing 'department' column, and the sample assignments (e.g. 'sales', 'product_management') are not supported by any visible source text, suggesting invented values.", "hallucination_observed": true},
    {"name": "documentation_completeness", "analytical_usefulness": 0.6, "source_groundedness": 0.8, "rationale": "Whether source_id/processed_date are present is a genuine compliance/documentation-risk axis directly relevant to the query, and derivable from actual field presence. Good grounding.", "hallucination_observed": false},
    {"name": "travel_asset_flag", "analytical_usefulness": 0.3, "source_groundedness": 0.7, "rationale": "Boolean travel flag is derivable from description but near-redundant with resource_purpose_intent's travel value and only marginally tied to decline reasons.", "hallucination_observed": false}
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.3,
  "source_groundedness": 0.6,
  "rationale": "The query asks about reasons and compliance risks in DECLINED expenses. Only documentation_completeness offers a real compliance-risk axis; the asset/provisioning/purpose columns describe what was purchased rather than why it was declined, and several restate each other (travel flag vs travel purpose; departmental_context vs department). Groundedness is mixed: description-based categorisations (asset_type, documentation_completeness) read soundly from the text, but departmental_context and some provisioning/purpose values assert specifics the shown source text does not support, indicating hallucination."
}

